exports[`runSecure --deep > runs Lynis over SSH, then ssh-audit and testssl.sh from this computer, and reports them 1`] = `
"## Deeper checks

Run with \`opscrew secure --deep\`. They change nothing on the server.

### Lynis 3.1.7

The server's own audit, run in a read-only container that leaves nothing behind.

Hardening index: **62** of 100.

| Result | Severity | Check | Where | Details |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Warn | Medium | Lynis hardening index is 65 or more |  | The Lynis hardening index is 62 of 100. |
| Warn | Medium | Lynis warning PKGS-7392 |  | Found one or more vulnerable packages. |
| Warn | Low | Lynis suggestion PKGS-7392 |  | Update your system with apt-get update, apt-get upgrade, apt-get dist-upgrade and/or unattended-upgrades |

Known noise, set apart and not counted:

| Check | Where | Details | Why it is set apart |
|---|---|---|---|
| Lynis warning PKGS-7388 |  | Can't find any security repository in /etc/apt/sources.list or sources.list.d directory | Lynis 3.1.7 does not read Ubuntu 24.04's deb822 sources (\`ubuntu.sources\`), so it misses the security repository that is there. |
| Lynis suggestion FILE-6310 |  | To decrease the impact of a full /home file system, place /home on a separate partition | Separate partitions for /home, /var or /tmp: a cloud server has one disk, and repartitioning it means rebuilding the server. |

### ssh-audit 3.9.0

The SSH service, audited from this computer.

| Result | Severity | Check | Where | Details |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Fail** | High | SSH meets ssh-audit's "Hardened Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS (version 2)" policy |  | The SSH server does not meet the policy: MACs differ. |
| Warn | Low | SSH MAC hmac-sha1 |  | hmac-sha1: using broken SHA-1 hash algorithm. |

Known noise, set apart and not counted:

| Check | Where | Details | Why it is set apart |
|---|---|---|---|
| SSH key exchange ecdh-sha2-nistp256 |  | ecdh-sha2-nistp256: using elliptic curves that are suspected as being backdoored by the U.S. National Security Agency. | A NIST curve: ssh-audit distrusts these on principle, no practical attack is known, and current clients choose the post-quantum or curve25519 exchange first. |

### testssl.sh 3.2.4

The TLS visitors see, audited from this computer.

| Result | Severity | Check | Where | Details |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Warn | Medium | TLS check security_headers | shop.example.com (Cloudflare's edge) | security_headers: none |

Known noise, set apart and not counted:

| Check | Where | Details | Why it is set apart |
|---|---|---|---|
| TLS check OCSP_stapling | shop.example.com (Cloudflare's edge) | OCSP_stapling: not offered | OCSP stapling: Let's Encrypt ended its OCSP service in 2025, so there is nothing to staple. |

---

Generated by OpsCrew 0.0.0-test. Run \`opscrew secure\` to refresh it. No secret values are included in this report.
"
`;

